cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Weight-Space Software Engineering (WSSE): circuit patches, wpgit and .weightpatch"
abstract: >-
  An LLM agent rewires small trained neural networks with exact, tested patches. Exact identities of
  (Leaky)ReLU activations carry signals, gate, bound and switch inside a trained network; room comes
  from freeing channels by regression or growing them with zero outgoing weights. Patches compile
  logic into a cat GAN (odd-eyed cats), give a 2018 super-sampler a provable output bound, resolve a
  fine-tune merge conflict with a self-checking routed union, and fix a classifier with a local
  exception. Patches are hash-pinned, self-testing text files that wpgit builds, tests in context,
  merge-checks and rebases under git.
